.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-GET 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts get
.Nd print a field of a ticket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts get
.Ar id
.Ar field
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command prints the values of a field of a ticket, one per line,
in the form they are stored in the index:
values of enum and set fields in lower case, and numbers without their unit.
Besides the fields described in
.Xr lbts-fields 5 ,
the
.Ar field
can be
.Ql title ,
.Ql id
for the full ID of the ticket, or
.Ql number .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 1 if the field is not set, or if there is no such ticket or field.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if [ "$(lbts get 42 status)" = closed ]; then ...
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
